
                                  HAMLOG
                                  ======
                                  
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
HAMLOG is a station log keeping program for the PSION SERIES 3 organiser.
It will store date, start time, end time, band, mode, power, station
details and notes. When required the program will output a text file of
the log entries to the internal memory.

   YOU CAN TRY THIS SOFTWARE FOR A PERIOD OF 28 DAYS AFTER WHICH YOU MUST
                 REGISTER IF YOU WISH TO KEEP USING IT.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

Installation
------------
The program comprises two files HAMLOG.OPA and HAML3.OPA, only one of the 
programs is needed for installation. HAMLOG is for the series 3a and HAML3
is for the series 3. If you received the program via a BBS these files,
along with some document files will be zipped into a file called HAMLOG.ZIP.
The zip file must be un-archived into the original files before it can be
installed on the PSION series 3.

To install the program copy the appropriate file to the \APP directory on
your PSION, and install the program into the main screen using the PSION-I
command. The file can be loaded to any local drive as required.

Files
-----
The program generates 3 files, one keeps the log entries, one keeps the 
default settings and the last keeps the password data. If you have a
registered version you can save the log file to drive A: or B: for additional
security.

If you should run into problems you can delete the password file and the
configuration file and rerun the software. This will recreate the required
files which can then be configured as required using the register and 
default options from the menu.

If the program does find a problem with the password or default file it will
erase them.

Operation
---------
When run the main screen shows information and a menu selection bar. You can
choose the required option or view the list by pressing TAB.

LOG - this option starts a log entry and will display the data entry screens,
      you can enter the appropriate data and move down the entries with the
      cursor key. When entries are correct you can press enter and move to
      the next screen.
      
      When complete the main menu shows. If you select LOG again the 
      log entry screen will show and allow the end time to be added.
      
      The registered version allows all previous entries for the current
      record to be amended as required.
      
      If you have completed an entry - and have made an error, you can load
      the logfile using the PSION database program in ROM and edit the last
      entry. YOU SHOULD ONLY EVER EDIT THE LAST ENTRY AS EDITING EARLIER
      ENTRIES SENDS THEM TO THE END OF THE FILE WHEN YOU SAVE THEM. THIS WILL
      RESULT IN THE LOG FILE BEING OUT OF ORDER.
      
      If you have version 1.01+ you can edit any entry if you have a file
      sorter. The date field of each entry has the time included so that
      sorting the database on field 1 will maintain the chronologial order
      of the log.

OUTPUT - This option outputs the finished log file in text format for 
      printing etc - the file is output to the \WRD directory on the
      internal memory. If you have the registered version you can output
      to a remote floppy drive on your PC via the link or print using a 
      parallel interface.

DEFAULTS - This option allows you to enter default information that will
      prefill on the data entry screens. You can enter your callsign,
      preferred band, output power and mode. If you have the registered
      version you can select a default drive for the logfile (good security)
      and you can select a GMT offset. The GMT offset will change the prefill
      time shown to that of GMT (from local). You can enter the number of
      hours ahead of GMT that your local time is.
      
      You can change defaults at anytime, the program will close the default
      file and reload it. Defaults will not save if program is not registered
      and used after 1995.

REGISTRATION - If you register the software you will be able to use the 
      additional registered facilities, you will also receive a copy of the
      latest version of the software on 3.5" HD disk (if UK registered by
      post).

      When registering please 1) Include you registration fee
                              2) Your full name
                              3) Your full address.
      Selecting the register option will display some information screens
      followed by the main registration screen, where you can enter your
      full name and password. When registered the software will show your
      name on the main screen.

REGISTRATION is primarily for the UK, users outside the UK should write for
      registration prices and details.

REGISTRATION PAYMENT please to Mr F Creese, PO Box 2224, Ferndown, BH22 8YY
                     ENGLAND. Use registered post if you want extra security.
                     Please send cash, UK Cheques or Eurocheques).
      
SECURITY
--------
      When the logfile becomes large you should copy it to another device
      and then HAMLOG will generate a new file. Before doing this you can
      print your log and file it for future use. If you make sure you save
      or copy your current log you can copy across an old log to output,
      remembering to re-load the new log afterwards.
      
      HAMLOG only works with one log file - be careful not to delete or
      copy over it by mistake. Also remember that backups of the logfile
      should be made to prevent loss due to equipment failure or other
      problems.
      
